// `"ab" * 3` — string repetition. Every other lane of this repository answers it, INCLUDING v3's
// own bridge, and only the executor refused: `Mul on String ab and Int 3`. That is invariant I-3
// between the two lanes of one compiler, and it is not hypothetical —
// `tests/conformance/indent-block-statements.ssc` builds its indentation with `" " * depth` and was
// the corpus's last exec-side DIFF, correct on the bridge and dead here.
//
// THE ZERO AND NEGATIVE ROWS ARE THE POINT OF HAVING MORE THAN ONE. Both give the empty string, and
// that was measured on the three answering lanes rather than taken from Scala's documentation,
// because the value the corpus's callers see is the one that matters.
//
// This fixture runs on the DEFAULT front through `ssc3 run` — the executor — which is where the
// defect was; `exec-gate.sh` then runs the same file on both lanes and compares them.
val neg = -1
println("ab" * 3)
println("[" + ("-" * 0) + "]")
println("[" + ("ab" * neg) + "]")
println("|" + (" " * 4) + "|")
